,title,link,text,language,family
0,Sino-Tibetan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sino-Tibetan_languages,"Sino-Tibetan (also referred to as Trans-Himalayan) is a family of more than 400 languages, second only to Indo-European in number of native speakers. Around 1.4 billion people speak a Sino-Tibetan language. The vast majority of these are the 1.3 billion native speakers of Sinitic languages.",Newar,Sino-Tibetan
1,"Tibetan Meditation Music, Soothing Music, Relaxing Music... - YouTube",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rmPmq-HlG5g,"Get the new Yellow Brick Cinema iOS app for a 7-day FREE trial: https://apple.co/30uHqHeTibetan Meditation Music, Soothing Music, Relaxing Music Meditation",Newar,Sino-Tibetan
2,Newar language,https://grokipedia.com/page/Newar_language,"The Newar language, a Sino-Tibetan language of the Tibeto-Burman family, features a nominal morphology characterized by inflectional marking primarily for case and number, with limited other categories such as animacy distinctions influencing case assignment.",Newar,Sino-Tibetan
3,Newar,https://accentnetwork.com/newar/,"Newar (Nepal Bhasa), spoken by around 840,000 people in Nepal, is part of the Sino-Tibetan language family. It is culturally significant among the Newar community.",Newar,Sino-Tibetan
4,Glottolog 5.3 - Sino-Tibetan,https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/sino1245,collapse all. Sino-Tibetan (519). Newar (3). Eastern Newari. Badikhel Pahari.,Newar,Sino-Tibetan
5,All In The Language Family: The Sino-Tibetan Languages,https://www.babbel.com/en/magazine/sino-tibetan-language-family,"Sino-Tibetan languages are also known as Trans-Himalayan. This might offer a clearer picture of where the languages are spoken: all over China, Burma, Tibet and across the Himalayas to small parts of India, Nepal and Bhutan.",Newar,Sino-Tibetan
6,Sino-Tibetan Branches Project (STBP) by Andy Hsiu,https://sites.google.com/site/sinotibetanbranches/,"Introduction Welcome to Andy Hsiu's Sino-Tibetan Branches Project (STBP) site, an online encyclopedia covering the branches of the Sino-Tibetan language family.",Newar,Sino-Tibetan
7,Ethnic origin of Newar & Tharu in Nepal,https://eastasiaorigin.blogspot.com/2022/04/ethnic-origin-of-newar-tharu.html,"They were originally Sino-Tibetan people related to the Kirat people in eastern Nepal. Sometime before 560 BC, the Tharu people migrated to Greater Lumbini in southern Nepal.",Newar,Sino-Tibetan
8,Sino-Tibetan language of central-eastern Nepal - Wikidata,https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q33979,Newar language. Newah Bhaye. Newari.,Newar,Sino-Tibetan
9,Egophoric Attitudes and Questions in Kathmandu Newar,https://publikationen.uni-tuebingen.de/xmlui/handle/10900/83154,Kathmandu Newar (Sino-Tibetan) has an egophoric verb marking system: an egophoric (or conjunct) verb form co-occurs with first person in declaratives and second person in inter- rogatives.,Newar,Sino-Tibetan
